PROGRAM DESCRIPTION: This program is designed to perform structured information extraction from scientific text, specifically targeting experimental data related to nanomaterials with enzyme-like activities (nanozymes). The core component is the `UniversalExtractor` class, which acts as a task-agnostic agent built on the DSPy framework. It wraps a `dspy.ChainOfThought` module, initialized with a specific `signature_class` that defines the schema of the data to be extracted (e.g., fields for catalyst formula, kinetic parameters like $K_m$ and $V_{max}$, reaction conditions like pH and temperature, and substrate types).

When executed via the `forward` method, the program takes a `document_text` (such as a research paper abstract or full text) as input. The underlying Chain-of-Thought model analyzes the text to identify relevant experimental sections and extracts values corresponding to the defined signature fields. As demonstrated in the provided examples, the program processes chemistry and materials science papers to output a structured list of `Experiment` objects, capturing quantitative metrics and qualitative conditions for peroxidase or catalase-like activities described in the literature. It also includes methods to save and load the configured agent state.
