Figure S6. pH-dependent POD-like activity of PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs. 50 μL PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs (100 μg mL<sup>−1</sup>) coincubated with 50 μL TMB liquid substrate system at different pH buffers for 30 min and the absorbance at 652 nm (n=3) was measured. Mean values and error bars are defined as mean and s.d., respectively.

Figure S7. Kinetics for POD-like activities of a) PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs to H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> substrate; b) PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs to TMB substrate; c) PtFe NRs to H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> substrate; d) PtFe NRs to TMB substrate; e) Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NPs to H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> substrate; f) Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NPs to TMB substrate. Error bars represent the standard error derived from three independent measurements. Mean values and error bars are defined as mean and s.d., respectively.

Figure S8. a) Wavelength dependent absorption value change of the UV-vis spectra at 652 nm for PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs based catalytic reaction system (50 mW cm<sup>−2</sup>, 5 min). b) SPR spectrum of PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs.

Figure S9. Comparison of the influence of SPR effect and thermal effect on catalytic reaction. 0.5 mL PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs (100 µg mL<sup>−1</sup>) were incubated with TMB liquid substrate system (50 µL) for 20 min at different conditions (0 °C-dark, 0 °C-NIR (1 W cm<sup>−2</sup>), 37 °C-dark). Then the absorbance values at 652 nm were detected. *P < 0.01, **P < 0.005, ***P < 0.001.

Figure S10. ESR spectra of O<sub>2</sub><sup>•−</sup> generation in the presence of H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> and PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs with or without NIR laser irradiation. (I: H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>; II: H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>-NIR; III: PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs+H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>; IV: PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs+H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>-NIR 1.5 min; V: PtFe@Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> NRs+H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>-NIR 3 min).

