PROGRAM DESCRIPTION: This program is an information extraction agent designed to parse scientific literature and convert unstructured text into structured experimental data. It leverages a Chain-of-Thought reasoning framework to analyze document text, specifically targeting experimental parameters and results within the fields of nanotechnology and biochemistry. The system initializes with a defined signature class that dictates the output schema, allowing it to identify and extract specific details such as catalyst composition, kinetic constants (e.g., $K_m$, $V_{max}$), reaction conditions (e.g., pH, temperature), and activity types (e.g., peroxidase-like activity). By processing the input text through this reasoning pipeline, the agent produces a standardized list of experiment objects, facilitating the automated aggregation and analysis of scientific findings from diverse research papers.
